From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:31:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(i18n): translate the desktop integration

Motivation: the tray, notification, metered-connection and Places strings
were English only.

Changes: their translations appended to po/pt_BR.po, and new catalogues for
pl, fr, de, es, ja, ko, zh_CN and zh_TW holding these strings and the four
existing ones the new interface reuses (Quit, Preferences and two
configuration messages). KDE's own word is used for Places in each
language. The desktop entries gain GenericName, Comment and Keywords in the
same eight languages.

Validation: msgfmt -c on every catalogue; the {account} placeholder is in
every translation; the strings read in a pt_BR Plasma session.

Limitations: the Flatpak manifests still install pt_BR only; translated by
the packager, not yet read by native speakers.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (branch order299 of the edition's DriveSync fork)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
